<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="137" project="spaarke-ontology-platform-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Per-node create/update/delete endpoints can still change or delete nodes of a system playbook (#1498): apply the task 133 guard without breaking the deploy tooling</title>
    <phase>8 Remaining cleanup and repairs</phase>
    <gate>after #1497 (task 133) review</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>BFF endpoints; protects live system playbooks; may touch the deploy path.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>S1</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>Own worktree off origin/master after #1497 merges (reuses its guard); own PR.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>133</deps>
    <tags>bff-api,ai,bug,separate-pr</tags>
    <estimated-effort>3-4 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Close the remaining path by which a system playbook's nodes can be changed outside the repo: the per-node endpoints in NodeEndpoints.cs.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE backend engineer.</role>
  <goal>No API path can create, update or delete a node of a protected playbook (the task 133 predicate), unless it is the sanctioned deploy path, and the deploy tooling still works.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Found by task 133 (PR #1497) and filed as #1498. Task 133 guards the Designer canvas save and the JIT sync through NodeService.EnsureCanvasSyncAllowedAsync. The per-node create/update/delete endpoints in NodeEndpoints.cs are not guarded. First establish (evidence, grep plus the deploy recipe) whether any deploy script (Deploy-Playbook*.ps1, the JPS deploy recipe, scripts/) uses these endpoints or writes Dataverse directly. That decides the design: guard them outright, or allow a deploy-only caller.
Evidence from the #1497 review (2026-10-09): every deploy and patch script (Deploy-Playbook.ps1, Create-DefaultPlaybook.ps1, Fix-SummarizeForChatPlaybookFK.ps1, Patch-PlaybookQueryFetchXml.ps1 and the retired notification scripts) writes the Dataverse Web API directly; nothing in scripts/ or the clients calls /api/ai/playbooks/{id}/nodes. So guarding them outright breaks no deploy path (re-verify on current master).
Also in scope (review K3): CreateNodeAsync / UpdateNodeAsync write request.ConfigJson verbatim, so a node created or updated through these endpoints has no `__canvasNodeId`, and task 133's node rule would then lock that user-authored playbook. Make these endpoints keep or stamp the marker for user playbooks, with a test.</background>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">Reuse the task 133 predicate; no second definition of "protected". Fail closed. A test per endpoint fails on the old code. If deploy tooling uses these endpoints, do not break it: bring the design choice to the main session before coding. Own worktree off origin/master after #1497 merges, own PR, do not merge. BFF hygiene per root CLAUDE.md section 10. Never use --no-verify or bare git stash. You cannot write .claude/. No parking. Closes #1498.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Create, update and delete of a node on a protected playbook are refused (409 playbook_read_only), with zero Dataverse writes; tests fail on the old code.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">User-authored playbooks are unaffected (regression tests).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The deploy path is proven still working (evidence recorded), or the PR states that it never used these endpoints.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">#1498 closed by the PR; CI green.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Created 2026-10-09 by the main session from #1498 (task 133 finding; no-parking rule).</notes>

  <execution><skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill></execution>
</task>
